      "id": "claim_7deb11bb36054dddaa972213c7c36033",
      "statement": "Two Claude Code hooks for the brain loop ship inside `rusty-cli` and are installed by `rusty-cli hooks install` (scripts to `~/.rusty/hooks/`, entries added to `~/.claude/settings.json` idempotently with every other entry kept; `status` and `uninstall` exist): in a working directory whose `.mcp.json` names a rusty server, the PreToolUse hook blocks a Write or Edit under that directory until the transcript holds a `mcp__rusty__brain_ask` tool use whose result was not an error, and the Stop hook refuses a stop once (`stop_hook_active` passes the retry) when files were written and no non-error `brain_decide` or `brain_no_decision` follows; both fail open without jq or a readable transcript; a corpus test runs the shipped scripts.",
